  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1032 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nAttention will quickly turn to a pair of systems to our south and \nwest. A deep positively titled upper low will descend over \nSouthern California late Monday into Tuesday. At the same time, \nHurricane Polo is expected to be making landfall over southern \nBaja California. The main upper through flow orientation would be \nenough on its own to bring a large fetch of Pacific moisture over \nour area, however this will also be combined with it \"sweeping up\"\nthe remnant moisture from Hurricane Polo. Timing remains somewhat\nuncertain, but areas along the TX/NM border would see the first \nof the associated precipitation Monday evening, with rain \ngradually shifting eastward with the progression of the \naforementioned through. Tuesday evening into early Wednesday\nmorning looks to be the period that will see the heaviest and \nmost widespread rainfall across the entire forecast area. GFS/NAM \ndevelops the dry slot sooner and thus an earlier end time \nWednesday morning, while ECMWF remains more optimistic with\nregards to rain persisting for longer. Respective GFS/ECMWF ensembles\nare similar to their deterministic counterparts. It remains too \nearly to be overly specific and everything will be monitored \nclosely in the coming days. A drier pattern looks to develop \nthereafter into next weekend.",
